Triggers: 

When we make changes in the git we come back and do it manually but that’s not how its done so we use triggers here 
Its similar to Cron jobs in Linux 

We have 5 types 

Trigger builds remotely (e.g., from scripts): From scrips if we use curl command and post the API and build the job we use this trigger 

Build after other projects are built: Suppose we have 1 project ex test-1 its upstream and test-2 is downstream job means only after test 1 is built it will trigger test-2 so test-1 will be primary that execution will trigger test-2. So first upstream will execute that will execute downstream job 

Build periodically: In cron we set * * * * * this means trigger the jobs every one minute similarly irrespective of the changes in the git file it will run on the iteration set

GitHub hook trigger for GITScm polling: Also called as web hooks. Similar to Poll SCM but difference is Once there is a change in git hub it directly run the build will not wait for that minute time difference.

Poll SCM: If we make any changes in Github this will try to fetch the info from Git if and only if there is any changes in Git file it will execute the jobs it not it will not execute the Build. So it checks every 1 minute and if there is a different it triggers the build of no no build 



