ADD behavior

1. Local .tar archive → ADD can extract it
For example:
httpd-2.4.68.tar.gz → using ADD → extracted into a folder

2. HTTP/HTTPS URL → ADD downloads the file
If you give ADD a Tomcat URL ending in .tar.gz, Docker downloads it and places the downloaded file in the destination.
It does not automatically mean it will extract the URL download.

Local tar archive + ADD → can extract
HTTP/HTTPS URL + ADD → downloads the file
Therefore, ADD does not create a ZIP file from an HTTP link. It downloads whatever file the URL provides.

